  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>guselkumab</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L04AC16</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Yao Z et al. 2018</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>patients with moderate to severe plaque psoriasis</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>guselkumab</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_guselkumab/Guselkumab_Yao2018_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>apparent clearance</td><td>0.516</td><td>L/day</td><td><small>CL/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>apparent volume of distribution</td><td>13.5</td><td>L</td><td><small>V/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>absorption rate constant</td><td>1.11</td><td>day-1</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr><tr><td>elimination half-life</td><td>18.1</td><td>days</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr></table><h4>About guselkumab</h4><p>Guselkumab is a monoclonal antibody that acts as an interleukin inhibitor, belonging to the immunosuppressant class of medicines. It is an approved medicine and has also been investigated for further uses.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15708315\">Wikidata Q15708315</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Guselkumab\">Guselkumab</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Yao Z et al. (2018). Population Pharmacokinetic Modeling of Guselkumab, a Human IgG1λ Monoclonal Antibody Targeting IL-23, in Patients with Moderate to Severe Plaque Psoriasis. <i>Journal of clinical pharmacology 58(5):61